            <ArticleTitle>The semeiology of autonomic pain: terminology and methods.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>39-41</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The morphological and functional structures underlying visceral sensations are discussed in order to identify the grounds for a semeiography of visceral pain. Special emphasis is given to the recent knowledge on fine afferent nerve fibres, central regulation of painful afferent paths and neurocybernetic mechanisms controlling pain threshold.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
